        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>For recording the raw card-level result of a single Cardiff acuity card test, expressed as the identifier of the finest card on which a reliable preferential-looking response was observed.&#xD;
&#xD;
The Cardiff acuity test is a preferential-looking test that uses vanishing-optotype pictures (e.g. fish, house, duck,&#xD;
  car, boat, train) printed at decreasing stroke widths on a sequence of cards. The result is conventionally reported as&#xD;
   the card identifier (LVA, LVB, A–M) rather than as a Snellen, decimal or logMAR value, because the conversion to a VA&#xD;
   notation depends on the testing distance and on the published card-to-acuity lookup for the edition of the test used.</purpose>
      <use>- Slot this cluster into the Test-specific results SLOT of the visual acuity archetype when the Cardiff acuity test&#xD;
  has been used. The card identifier captured here is the primary, raw result of the test.&#xD;
  - Any conversion of this card identifier to a notation-based VA value (decimal, logMAR, Snellen ratio, cycles per&#xD;
  degree) should be recorded in the Derived Result cluster of the parent VA archetype, together with the testing&#xD;
  distance and chart edition needed to interpret it.</use>
      <misuse />
